    "title": "Cheque number served with account detail",
    "description": "A cheque number field next to its value appears in the response body. A cheque leaf number with the account lets someone present or dispute a payment they never received, and it is a stable identifier that survives reissue.",
    "remediation": "Mask the leaf number and show only the cleared status of the cheque.",
    "limitation": "One response body. It matches the cheque word and a six-to-nine digit number, not the amount.",
    "scopeT": "One response body. It matches the cheque word and a six-to-nine digit number, not the amount.",
    "fp": "A page that explains how to order a cheque book, with no number, is not reported.",
    "recordDesc": "A cheque number field next to its value in a response gives every reader the same view the bank has internally: A cheque leaf number with the account lets someone present or dispute a payment they never received, and it is a stable identifier that survives reissue.",
    "applicability": "Cheque status, clearing and branch-service pages.",
    "risk": "Cheque numbers support forged stop-payment requests and dispute fraud.",
    "why": "The leaf number is a bearer-style reference to a physical instrument.",
    "fix": [
      "Show only the cleared or pending status.",
      "Require branch authentication for leaf-level detail."
    ],
    "verifyT": "Open the cheque status page and confirm no leaf number is returned.",
