    "description": "A KYC block with a document reference value appears in the response body. The reference ties a real identity document to the account, and with the document type it is enough to impersonate the customer at a branch or in a call centre.",
    "remediation": "Return only a masked reference and the verification status, and keep the full number in the encrypted KYC store.",
    "limitation": "One response body. It matches the KYC wording and a document reference value, not the document image.",
    "scopeT": "One response body. It matches the KYC wording and a document reference value, not the document image.",
    "fp": "A page that says verification is complete, with no reference, is not reported.",
    "recordDesc": "A KYC block with a document reference value in a response gives every reader the same view the bank has internally: The reference ties a real identity document to the account, and with the document type it is enough to impersonate the customer at a branch or in a call centre.",
    "applicability": "Onboarding status, profile and branch-service pages.",
    "risk": "A document number is a durable identity credential; it survives password changes and device resets.",
    "why": "The KYC reference is the link between an account and a real-world identity.",
    "fix": [
