    "description": "An embed element with a source appears in the response body. The embed element loads a plugin document that the page cannot sandbox or inspect, and plugin content has historically carried its own script-execution surface.",
    "remediation": "Replace the embed with a sandboxed iframe from a reviewed origin, or remove the plugin content.",
    "limitation": "One response body. It matches the embed element and its source, not whether the source is trusted.",
    "scopeT": "One response body. It matches the embed element and its source, not whether the source is trusted.",
    "fp": "An embed that points at a same-origin, reviewed document is a weaker finding.",
    "recordDesc": "An embed element with a source in a response gives every reader the same view the bank has internally: The embed element loads a plugin document that the page cannot sandbox or inspect, and plugin content has historically carried its own script-execution surface.",
    "applicability": "Legacy PDF viewers, media players and document preview pages.",
    "risk": "Plugin content runs outside the page's script policy, so the CSP does not constrain it.",
    "why": "An embed is a document the page cannot govern; an iframe with sandbox is the modern equivalent.",
    "fix": [
      "Replace the embed with a sandboxed iframe.",
      "If the plugin must stay, pin its source and remove script capability from it."
